# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore  -  RetailAPOLLO
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the repo had none, which is the reason six
# __pycache__ directories, a .pytest_cache and twelve LaTeX intermediates
# had accumulated and needed a manual sweep.  Deleting them once fixes the
# symptom; ignoring them fixes the cause.
#
# RULE OF THUMB used below: ignore anything a COMMAND can regenerate from
# committed inputs, and never ignore anything a command cannot.  That is why
# Data/abstracted/, Data/dashboard/ and Data/research_record/ are absent
# from this file - they are committed inputs (the text-free aggregates, the
# display bundle a hosted copy renders, and the frozen research record).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Python bytecode / tooling caches (regenerated on next run) ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- virtual environments ----
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- LaTeX intermediates -------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by `pdflatex` on every compile.  The .pdf is NOT ignored: the
# deck is a deliverable and a reader without a TeX install still needs it.
*.aux
*.log
*.nav
*.out
*.snm
*.toc
*.vrb
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.bbl
*.blg

# ---- raw / private data --------------------------------------------------
# The raw store holds post TEXT and author handles, so it must never be
# committed.  Data/processed/ is derived (rebuildable from a hydrate) and
# large, so it stays local too; Data/abstracted/ is the committed form.
Data/raw/
Data/processed/
Data/cache/
# run logs and the small pipeline reports (Reports/) are machine-local
Reports/*
!Reports/.gitkeep

# ---- OS noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- machine-local pipeline ledgers ---------------------------------------
# These two files MEASURE THIS MACHINE: how long each stage takes here, and
# what each forum costs when crawled from here.  Committing them would plan
# one machine's run with another's numbers - a slower machine would inherit
# a page allowance it cannot afford inside the ~10-minute run ceiling
# (PIPELINE_BUDGET_S) and quietly overrun on every run.  Each falls back to
# a bootstrap prior in src/config.py and re-measures itself within one run,
# so a fresh clone loses nothing but one run's worth of precision.
# See src/pipeline_budget.py.
Data/reference/pipeline_stage_times.json
Data/reference/reddit_comments_cost.json

# Backfill progress ledger (tools/backfill_reddit.py): which historical
# chunks THIS machine has already pulled. Local operational state - the
# data it describes lands in data/raw, which is never committed either.
Data/reference/reddit_backfill_progress.json

# AI layer: local-only text + operational state (never committed - the
# same text-free boundary as data/raw)
Data/reference/agentic_samples.jsonl
Data/reference/agentic_scan_ledger.json
Data/reference/nb10_sample_texts.jsonl
# Ledger snapshots are machine-local recovery state and contain copies of
# the text files above; they never belong in a commit.
Data/reference/_backups/

# ---- .env is NOT tracked (supersedes the earlier decision) ----
# It was previously committed so that credentials travelled with the
# repository to the second machine. Hosting the dashboard ends that: a
# deploy clones the repository onto third-party infrastructure, and the
# file holds the FetchLayer key, the Reddit account password, the X
# bearer token, and the gateway credentials. Distribution now has to be
# manual - copy .env between machines out of band; a fresh clone starts
# from example.env.
#
# The superseded values remain readable in the history that already
# exists, so treat every key that has ever appeared here as burned until
# it is rotated.
.env

# Only the evaluation notebook is tracked. The delivery itself is
# multi-GB unaggregated raw post text: oversized for git history, and
# raw text is exactly what the text-free commit rule exists to keep out
# of the repository. Both case spellings are listed because gitignore
# matching follows core.ignorecase (true on Windows, false on Linux);
# a single-case rule would stop protecting the folder on a Linux clone.

# Staging area for files retired from the project (review, then delete).
_to_delete/

# ---- workstation marker (never committed, by design) ---------------------
# Its presence enables the dashboard's pipeline-run controls. A hosted clone
# cannot have it, so a public viewer is never offered a button that fetches,
# spends API credit, or calls a Bloomberg Terminal. Created by
# tools/publish_dashboard.py; see LOCAL_CONTROLS in dashboard.py.

# Data/dashboard/ is deliberately ABSENT from this file. Like
# Data/abstracted/, it is a committed INPUT: the finished display frames the
# hosted dashboard reads, staged by tools/publish_dashboard.py, which refuses
# to publish anything carrying FORBIDDEN_COLS.

# ---- material that is not needed to run the pipeline ---------------------
# Reference Materials/archive/ holds the long-form docs, old research
# notebooks and the old parameter reference. Reference Materials/research.ipynb
# is the one committed write-up.
Reference Materials/archive/
# generated proposals from the keyword auditor (review, then apply)
Data/reference/keyword_suggestions/
Data/reference/subreddit_panel.json
# per-copy settings overrides (pipeline controls etc.)
Code/config/settings.local.csv
